---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Service | Contractor Ledger';
const description = 'Terms for using Contractor Ledger estimating calculators, including estimate limits and user assumptions.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 lg:py-14 space-y-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-text-muted" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-text-primary font-semibold">Terms of Service</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-text-primary tracking-tight font-headline">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted">
        Last updated: October 20, 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-border-default p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-subtle space-y-6 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          1. Using the Calculators
        </h2>
        <p>
          Contractor Ledger provides free calculators for estimating job prices, labor costs, margin, break-even rates, material markups, and project costs. Use the results for planning and review.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          2. Estimates and Your Assumptions
        </h2>
        <p>
          Results are estimates based on the values you enter and the formulas shown on the site. They are not a quote, a guaranteed bid, a promise of profit, or legal, tax, accounting, or engineering advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Check that your costs, hours, quantities, overhead, and rates are complete and current for the job. The calculators cannot identify missing costs or verify supplier quotes, payroll assumptions, taxes, insurance, fees, or contract requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          3. Review Before You Bid
        </h2>
        <p>
          Review every estimate before sharing or relying on it. Actual costs and job results can differ from estimates, and the site does not guarantee commercial outcomes or profitability. Currency amounts are rounded to cents.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          4. Changes to the Site
        </h2>
        <p>
          The site, calculators, or formulas may change. Check the current calculation methods and assumptions before using a result.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
